{%- comment -%}
  Registry accessor (spec §17.2) — the single indirection every caller uses, so
  caching can be added in ONE place. The manifests are code, so the built registry
  only changes on deploy; platformOS's {% cache %} auto-invalidates on any view
  change (= on deploy), making it the correct future cache primitive here.

  Currently a direct pass-through to registry/build (the registry is small; per-
  request build is within the pipeline budget). When profiling (§17.3) warrants
  it, wrap the build in {% cache 'mcp_registry', expire: N %} here — no caller
  changes. Kept uncached for now to avoid stale/escaping edge cases before the
  suite (task-1.10) locks behavior.

  @return {object} { tools, excluded, count } — see registry/build
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  function reg = 'modules/mcp/commands/registry/build'
  return reg
%}
